clean_summary:
Da Dream! It's really good for those of us who are horrible at design. At an offsite two weeks ago, we had 71 people editing the same slide deck, and it went smoother than I expected! Design was very consistent across all slides.

By the way, it's so hard to keep track of what we are releasing externally when we are shipping fast and using different code names! And don't even get me started on model code names.

@claudeai: "Introducing Claude Design by Anthropic Labs: make prototypes, slides, and one-pagers by talking to Claude. Powered by Claude Opus 4.7, our most capable vision model. Available in research preview on the Pro, Max, Team, and Enterprise plans, rolling out throughout the day."

Amazing team. Excited to see what @bneyshabur and his crew build.

@bneyshabur announces the formation of MirendilAI with co-founders Harsh Mehta, Shayan Salehian, and Tara Rezaei. The company has secured a $200M seed round led by @a16z and @kleinerperkins, with additional investment from NVIDIA, aiming to accelerate science and technology.

MirendilAI focuses on self-accelerating AI research to speed up progress across all domains. The goal is to democratize this capability so more groups can pursue scientific innovation, reducing concentration of power in a few labs. The team includes 20 researchers and engineers from top institutions like Anthropic, xAI, Google DeepMind, and OpenAI, united by a passion for advancing science and building faster-moving technologies.

I'm shocked this didn't get more attention honestly. This is one of my favorite features and I was very ready for it to be out so I can talk about it.

I'm really having a hard time understanding X these days. Posts that I think should not get attention blow up (mine included) and then there are ones that I think are the big unblockers but they don't make it all over the feed.

